---
import { mediaPath } from '@/constants';
const resetHr = { src: `${mediaPath}/reset-hr.png?alt=media` } as ImageMetadata;
const resetMin = { src: `${mediaPath}/reset-min.png?alt=media` } as ImageMetadata;
const resetSec = { src: `${mediaPath}/reset-sec.png?alt=media` } as ImageMetadata;
const resetDate = { src: `${mediaPath}/reset-date.png?alt=media` } as ImageMetadata;
const resetMonth = { src: `${mediaPath}/reset-mon.png?alt=media` } as ImageMetadata;
const resetYear = { src: `${mediaPath}/reset-year.png?alt=media` } as ImageMetadata;
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
---

<div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm md:text-lg">
	<div class="col-span-3 sm:col-span-2">
		<ol class="list-outside list-decimal space-y-6 pl-6 sm:pl-9">
			<li class="grid-cols-3">
				<span class="font-medium">Waking Up the Watch:</span>
				Press the button once to wake up the watch. Upon waking up, the watch will first display the current time.
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="font-medium">Entering Reset Mode:</span>
				To make adjustments to the watch settings, perform a long press and hold the button for approximately 1.5 seconds.
				This will take you to the RESET mode. The first thing you can reset is the hour, meaning you are in "reset hour"
				mode.
				<ol class="mt-7 list-outside list-[lower-latin] space-y-5 pl-6 sm:pl-9">
					<li>
						<span class="font-medium">Adjusting the Hour:</span>
						<ol class="mt-1 list-outside list-[lower-roman] space-y-1 pl-6 sm:pl-9">
							<li>
								Once in RESET mode, the display will show “hr” (for few seconds), indicating that you can change the
								HOUR value
								<span class="font-medium">(Image 1).</span>
							</li>
							<li>
								Use short presses to increase the hour value.{' '}
								<span class="font-medium">Note:</span> The hour value will cycle back to 0 after reaching 23.
							</li>
							<li class="space-x-2">
								After you land on the desired hour value, confirm it by holding the button for approximately 1 second.
							</li>
						</ol>
						<li>
							This will now take you to the “reset minute” mode.{' '}
							<span class="font-medium">(Image 2)</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="font-medium">Adjusting the Minute</span>
							<ol class="mt-1 list-outside list-[lower-roman] space-y-1 pl-6 sm:pl-9">
								<li>
									Following the hour adjustment, the display will show “nin”. Due to the limitations of 7-segment
									displays, "min" for minutes is represented as “nin”.
								</li>
								<li>Use short presses to increase the minute value (just like the previous step).</li>
								<li>
									Once you've changed the desired minute value, confirm your selection with a long press by
									approximately pressing the button for 1 sec.
								</li>
							</ol>
						</li>
						<li>
							This will now take you the "reset seconds" mode{' '}
							<span class="font-medium">(Image 3).</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							Repeat the above steps to change the SECONDS, then DATE, MONTH, and YEAR values
							<span class="font-medium">(Image 4, 5, 6).</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="font-medium">Note:</span>
							If you wish to skip adjusting a particular component (e.g. the seconds, the year etc.), simply perform a long
							press (approx. 1 sec) to move on to the next component.
						</li>
					</li>
				</ol>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="font-medium">Exiting Reset Mode</span>
				After setting the YEAR value, the watch will automatically exit the RESET mode, and your adjustments will be saved.
				Note: If you wish to leave the RESET mode in the middle, just press long enough (2.5 sec) and release.
			</li>
		</ol>
		<p class="mt-6 font-medium">Notes :</p>
		<ol class="mt-5 mb-6 list-outside list-decimal space-y-1 pl-6 sm:pl-9">
			<li>
				The "Year" value rolls over after approaching 2100. This decision was made to make it easier on the fingers
				while manually resetting components with the button.
			</li>
			<li>Always make sure that you have set the correct values for each component before exiting the RESET mode.</li>
		</ol>
	</div>

	<div class="col-span-3 grid grid-cols-2 gap-8 sm:col-span-1 sm:grid-cols-1">
		<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4 text-xs sm:ml-auto sm:w-44 sm:items-end">
			<Image src={resetHr} alt="Reset Hour" class="aspect-square w-44" />
			<div class="w-full text-xs sm:w-44">
				<p class="font-medium">Image 1</p>
				<p>HOUR (hr): Now you can change the hour</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4 text-xs sm:ml-auto sm:w-44 sm:items-end">
			<Image src={resetMin} alt="Reset Minute" class="aspect-square w-44" />
			<div class="w-full text-xs sm:w-44">
				<p class="font-medium">Image 2</p>
				<p>MINUTE (Shown as nin - as it is hard to represent in 7 segment): Now you can change the minute.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4 text-xs sm:ml-auto sm:w-44 sm:items-end">
			<Image src={resetSec} alt="Reset Second" class="aspect-square w-44" />
			<div class="w-full text-xs sm:w-44">
				<p class="font-medium">Image 3</p>
				<p>SECOND (sec) : Now you can change the seconds.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4 text-xs sm:ml-auto sm:w-44 sm:items-end">
			<Image src={resetDate} alt="Reset Date" class="aspect-square w-44" />
			<div class="w-full text-xs sm:w-44">
				<p class="font-medium">Image 4</p>
				<p>DATE (date): Now you can change the date.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4 text-xs sm:ml-auto sm:w-44 sm:items-end">
			<Image src={resetMonth} alt="Reset Month" class="aspect-square w-44" />
			<div class="w-full text-xs sm:w-44">
				<p class="font-medium">Image 5</p>
				<p>MONTH (Shown as non - as it is hard to represent in 7 segment): Now you change the month.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4 text-xs sm:ml-auto sm:w-44 sm:items-end">
			<Image src={resetYear} alt="Reset Year" class="aspect-square w-44" />
			<div class="w-44">
				<p class="font-medium">Image 6</p>
				<p>YEAR (year ): Now you can change the year.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
